    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nRedesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it follows the new region-and-hash identity.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewrote the builder. It no longer counts owners or uses a sequence (dropped the `OwnerRepository` dependency entirely). It now sets `customerCode = REGION + \"-\" + HASH8` where:\n- **REGION** = region derived from the owner's postcode (via `CustomerCodeRegion` \u2192 `LocalityLookup.regionOf(city, postcode)`, which prefers the postcode and falls back to the city table, giving `UNKNOWN` for unmapped values).\n- **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`, where the telephone is the E.164 form (already normalized upstream by `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`).\n\n**`CustomerCodeRegion.java`** (new) \u2014 a small utility (mirroring `CustomerCodeCheckDigit`) that returns the REGION segment: the prefix of an assigned `customerCode`, else the postcode/city-derived region. Kept separate because OfficeFloor requires exactly one public method on a function class, and both `AssignCustomerCode` and the mapper need this logic.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the **locality** derivation moved onto the identity: `locality` now comes from `CustomerCodeRegion.of(owner)` (the REGION of the identity) instead of independently recomputing from city+postcode.\n\n**Automatically inherited** (no logic change needed, only javadoc/OpenAPI accuracy): the **membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its **check digit** (Luhn over the digits in the new code), and the **create audit record** (logs `customerCode`) all now reflect the new identity.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated `openapi.yml` descriptions/examples for `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality`, plus the relevant class javadocs.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` passes \u2014 `customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}` (audit confirmed e.g. `NSW-16E6609E`). **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures.",
